note <ECDH key agreement over X25519. The clean uniform interface; the per-env native implementation is selected at build time and hidden. Each platform delegates to its built-in X25519 (node / browser Web Crypto, rust x25519-dalek, swift CryptoKit, kotlin java.security). Keys and the shared secret are hex: the private key and public key are 32 bytes each, the shared secret is the raw 32-byte X25519 output. make-key-pair generates a matched pair together. shared-secret(my private, their public) equals shared-secret(their private, my public): that agreement is the whole point of ECDH. The interface is async to stay uniform with the rest of cryptography.>

load @cluesurf/base/code/native/cryptography/key-agreement
  find make-key-pair-bytes
  find compute-shared-secret

load @cluesurf/base/code/text/string
  find slice

form exchange-pair
  link private-key, like text
  link public-key, like text

task make-key-pair
  mark async
  like exchange-pair
  save raw
    call make-key-pair-bytes
      wait true
  send back
    make exchange-pair
      bind private-key
        call slice
          read raw
          mark 0
          mark 64
      bind public-key
        call slice
          read raw
          mark 64
          mark 128

task shared-secret
  mark async
  take private-key, like text
  take public-key, like text
  like text
  send back
    call compute-shared-secret
      read private-key
      read public-key
      wait true
